---
description: Core behavioral rules for every coding task — think, simplify, be surgical, verify
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

## Think Before Coding
State assumptions before implementing. Surface ambiguity and options — don't hide confusion.
Define what "working" looks like before writing any code (which field renders, what the check confirms).

## Simplicity First
Write the minimum code that solves the problem. No unrequested abstractions, features, or future-proofing.
Three similar lines is better than a premature abstraction.

## Surgical Changes
Touch only what the request requires. Every changed line must trace back to the ask.
Match existing file style and patterns exactly. Clean only your own mess.

## Goal-Driven Execution
Run `npm run typecheck && npm run lint` after every non-trivial change.
Do not claim a feature works without verifying actual browser output.
